  "result": "I've written the NRS_484B_250_4_o1 rule and its witnesses, and the gate returned **OK** on the second of six runs (13 witnesses). The first run failed to build because of one extra closing parenthesis.\n\n**How the rule reads:**\n- **When it applies:** the subject's footprint enters an intersection X now, and at the previous observation it was on a carrier c that enters X. An uncovered traffic signal that governs c or X must be inoperative at that moment.\n- **What it requires:** at the observation just before the entry, a search back through earlier observations must find a complete halt at the right place, in the law's order:\n  1. at a stop line marking c (line ahead or at the reference point, body within 2 m);\n  2. otherwise before a crosswalk marking c (body off it, within 2 m);\n  3. otherwise just outside X (within 2 m).\n- **How the search ends:**\n  - A halt found first is compliant.\n  - Reaching the approach start or the subject's previous entry into X first is a violation.\n  - Reaching the start of the recording with neither is unknown.\n\n**Witnesses:** the seven planned scenes (forbid, permit, idle, blind, history_boundary, branch_1, branch_2), plus six I added so each branch of the rule is tested:\n- branch_3: re-entering X without a new halt;\n- branch_4: the signal governs X rather than c;\n- branch_5: crosswalk only, compliant;\n- branch_6: halting on the crosswalk;\n- branch_7: no mark, no halt;\n- branch_8: halting too far before the line.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- **Several entry carriers:** the duty applies through every carrier the subject entered from. Where carriers would give different verdicts, the rule says violated, which is stricter than the carrier contract (it says unknown). This only matters in a rare setup none of the witnesses covers.\n- **\"Off the mark\":** carried by \"body farther than 2 m from the mark\", since that distance is zero when the body overlaps the mark.\n- **No narrowings declared.**\n\n**For the plan:** the node claims the aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic`, but nothing in the obligation reads it. The record's own reading treats \"view of approaching traffic\" as just a place. The gate didn't flag it, but the plan may want to drop that claim.\n\nEverything is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
